{
	title: 'Trust-gated project instructions and plugin session lifetimes',
	spec: 'Project trust is one explicit user decision covering AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md, project skills, and native Hal plugins. Ask before the first instruction injection or plugin activation only when applicable material exists. Trust applies to the canonical project root and future content, not content hashes; no hash-based repeated approvals. Discover from the nearest Git root through the session cwd; outside Git use only cwd. Native project plugins live in .agents/plugins/hal and personal plugins in ~/.agents/plugins/hal. Trusted plugins retain unrestricted in-process authority, including around hooks; file-local and session-local effects remain optional conventions and helpers, not a sandbox. A project plugin directory stays active while at least one open session needs it and deactivates, removes hooks, stops watching and runs cleanup when the last session leaves or closes. Activation and deactivation are hook points. Reopening reactivates after remembered trust. Trust questions use the common durable form flow for terminal and web. Prompt assembly, inspection and change notices must not bypass trust. Portable plugins retain reviewed client/server synchronization without merging unrelated projects or sending nonportable files. Preserve existing Hal-home plugin files and history while integrating personal discovery. No catalog/add/find command is required. Keep trust-boundary and lifecycle regression coverage, including restart, concurrent sessions, cwd changes, newly appearing material, declined trust and canceled activation.',
